<title>SPAIN: New union labour proposals interesting - CEOE.</title>
<headline>New union labour proposals interesting - CEOE.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's CEOE employer organisation said on Wednesday that the trade unions new proposals for the reform of the labour market were interesting.</p>
<p>&quot;All the proposals are interesting,&quot; CEOE President Jose Maria Cuevas told journalists before unions and employers resumed talks after a break of several days.</p>
<p>Cuevas said the two sides were getting closer to an agreement and that talks would follow along the lines set by the unions' new proposal.</p>
<p>&quot;If they think that that is where we need to reach agreement for an accord, then I think we can go that way,&quot; Cuevas said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
